# Service Layer Patterns

## Service Architecture

### Service Organization
- Place all business logic in service classes under `app/Services/`
- Use dependency injection for service dependencies
- Follow single responsibility principle
- Implement proper error handling and validation

```php
// Good: Well-structured service with dependencies
class CourseService
{
    public function __construct(
        private CourseEnrollmentService $enrollmentService,
        private PaymentService $paymentService,
        private MediaService $mediaService
    ) {}

    public function createCourse(array $data): Course
    {
        return DB::transaction(function () use ($data) {
            $course = Course::create($data);
            $this->mediaService->handleCourseMedia($course, $data['media'] ?? []);
            return $course;
        }, 5);
    }
}
```

### Service Responsibilities
- **CourseService**: Course creation, updates, publishing logic
- **PaymentService**: Payment processing, revenue calculations
- **UserService**: User management, profile updates
- **InstructorService**: Instructor-specific business logic
- **StudentService**: Student enrollment, progress tracking
- **MediaService**: File uploads, storage management

## Business Logic Patterns

### Transaction Management
- Use database transactions for data integrity
- Implement proper rollback strategies
- Handle concurrent access scenarios
- Use appropriate transaction isolation levels

```php
// Good: Transaction with proper error handling
public function processCoursePurchase(array $data): PaymentHistory
{
    return DB::transaction(function () use ($data) {
        $payment = $this->createPayment($data);
        $this->enrollmentService->enrollStudent($data['user_id'], $data['course_id']);
        $this->calculateInstructorRevenue($payment);
        
        return $payment;
    }, 5);
}
```

### Data Validation
- Validate business rules in services
- Use form requests for input validation
- Implement custom validation rules
- Handle validation errors gracefully

```php
// Good: Business rule validation
public function enrollStudent(int $userId, int $courseId): Enrollment
{
    $user = User::findOrFail($userId);
    $course = Course::findOrFail($courseId);
    
    // Business rule validation
    if ($this->isAlreadyEnrolled($userId, $courseId)) {
        throw new BusinessException('User is already enrolled in this course');
    }
    
    if (!$course->isPublished()) {
        throw new BusinessException('Course is not available for enrollment');
    }
    
    return $this->createEnrollment($user, $course);
}
```

### Service Composition
- Compose services for complex operations
- Use service facades for common operations
- Implement service interfaces for testability
- Avoid circular dependencies

```php
// Good: Service composition pattern
class CourseManagementService
{
    public function __construct(
        private CourseService $courseService,
        private CourseSectionService $sectionService,
        private CourseLessonService $lessonService,
        private MediaService $mediaService
    ) {}

    public function createCompleteCourse(array $data): Course
    {
        $course = $this->courseService->createCourse($data);
        $this->sectionService->createSections($course, $data['sections']);
        $this->lessonService->createLessons($course, $data['lessons']);
        $this->mediaService->processCourseMedia($course, $data['media']);
        
        return $course;
    }
}
```

## Payment & Revenue Services

### Payment Processing
- Handle multiple payment gateways
- Implement proper error handling
- Use payment service abstraction
- Handle webhook processing

```php
// Good: Payment service abstraction
interface PaymentGatewayInterface
{
    public function processPayment(array $data): PaymentResult;
    public function handleWebhook(array $data): bool;
}

class StripeService implements PaymentGatewayInterface
{
    public function processPayment(array $data): PaymentResult
    {
        try {
            $charge = Stripe::charges()->create([
                'amount' => $data['amount'],
                'currency' => $data['currency'],
                'source' => $data['source'],
            ]);
            
            return new PaymentResult($charge);
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            throw new PaymentException('Payment processing failed: ' . $e->getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

### Revenue Calculation
- Calculate instructor commissions
- Handle platform revenue
- Implement payout logic
- Track revenue analytics

```php
// Good: Revenue calculation service
class RevenueService
{
    public function calculateCourseRevenue(Course $course, float $totalAmount): array
    {
        $instructorRevenue = $this->getInstructorRevenuePercentage();
        $platformRevenue = 100 - $instructorRevenue;
        
        return [
            'instructor_amount' => $totalAmount * ($instructorRevenue / 100),
            'platform_amount' => $totalAmount * ($platformRevenue / 100),
            'instructor_percentage' => $instructorRevenue,
            'platform_percentage' => $platformRevenue,
        ];
    }
}
```

## Course Management Services

### Course Creation
- Handle course creation workflow
- Manage course metadata
- Process course media
- Implement course validation

```php
// Good: Course creation service
class CourseService
{
    public function createCourse(array $data, User $instructor): Course
    {
        $this->validateCourseData($data);
        
        return DB::transaction(function () use ($data, $instructor) {
            $course = Course::create([
                'title' => $data['title'],
                'description' => $data['description'],
                'instructor_id' => $instructor->id,
                'status' => CourseStatusType::DRAFT,
            ]);
            
            $this->createCourseSections($course, $data['sections'] ?? []);
            $this->handleCourseMedia($course, $data['media'] ?? []);
            
            return $course;
        });
    }
}
```

### Course Publishing
- Implement course approval workflow
- Handle course status changes
- Manage course visibility
- Process course notifications

```php
// Good: Course publishing logic
public function publishCourse(Course $course): Course
{
    $this->validateCourseForPublishing($course);
    
    return DB::transaction(function () use ($course) {
        $course->update(['status' => CourseStatusType::PUBLISHED]);
        $this->notifyCoursePublished($course);
        $this->updateCourseVisibility($course);
        
        return $course;
    });
}
```

## User Management Services

### User Registration
- Handle user registration workflow
- Process email verification
- Manage user roles
- Handle social authentication

```php
// Good: User registration service
class UserService
{
    public function registerUser(array $data): User
    {
        $this->validateRegistrationData($data);
        
        return DB::transaction(function () use ($data) {
            $user = User::create([
                'name' => $data['name'],
                'email' => $data['email'],
                'password' => Hash::make($data['password']),
                'role' => UserType::STUDENT,
            ]);
            
            $this->sendVerificationEmail($user);
            $this->createUserProfile($user);
            
            return $user;
        });
    }
}
```

### Role Management
- Handle role transitions
- Manage permissions
- Process role-specific workflows
- Handle role-based access control

```php
// Good: Role management service
class RoleService
{
    public function promoteToInstructor(User $user): Instructor
    {
        $this->validateInstructorPromotion($user);
        
        return DB::transaction(function () use ($user) {
            $instructor = Instructor::create([
                'user_id' => $user->id,
                'status' => 'pending_approval',
            ]);
            
            $user->update(['role' => UserType::INSTRUCTOR]);
            $this->notifyInstructorApplication($instructor);
            
            return $instructor;
        });
    }
}
```

## Media & File Services

### File Upload Handling
- Process file uploads securely
- Handle different file types
- Implement file validation
- Manage file storage

```php
// Good: File upload service
class MediaService
{
    public function uploadCourseMedia(Course $course, array $files): array
    {
        $uploadedFiles = [];
        
        foreach ($files as $file) {
            $this->validateFile($file);
            $path = $this->storeFile($file, 'courses/' . $course->id);
            $uploadedFiles[] = $this->createMediaRecord($course, $file, $path);
        }
        
        return $uploadedFiles;
    }
}
```

